                <pb facs="1126" n="1046" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg1046"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Leishman to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-08-21"><hi rendition="#italic">August 21,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Leishman reports that, the Sultan having sent his secretary begging Mr.
                    Leishman to overlook the discourtesy of the grand vizier, and at the same time
                    giving assurance that the questions immediately at issue would all be settled,
                    and that His Imperial Majesty had sent the most emphatic instructions to the
                    grand vizier to receive Mr. Leishman at all times in a manner befitting the
                    dignity of the representative of a great power, he has consented to resume
                    ordinary relations.</p>
                <p>Having been forced to assume a strong position, Mr. Leishman regrets that the
                    settlement was not based upon broader principles, but states that the action
                    taken will undoubtedly have a good effect; that in view of wishes expressed in
                    the Department’s cabled instructions, he deemed it wise to close the affair on
                    an honorable basis and to avoid even the possibility of strained relations.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
